### 1. Register Audit (`W0`–`W9`): What’s Freed & What’s Tangled
In `qandyland-univac.js`, `w/a` currently stores `W0`–`W9`:
* **`W0` (Spawn Sector) & `W1` (Spawn Z):** Already superseded by `/a/gfxSpawn` and `/a/gfxSpawnZ` in `Xa` (with `W0`/`W1` kept as fallbacks). For 2029 worlds, these two registers are **free**.
* **`W4` (Map Lower Bounds):** `cylon-gfx.js` already reads `/a/gfxLowerBound`, while `UNIVAC` still reads `register['W4']` (defaulting to `"Dd"`). Moving `UNIVAC` to check `/a/gfxLowerBound` first (falling back to `W4`) frees up **`W4`** as well.
* **`W2` & `W3` (Player ID Odometer):** Still actively used by `tickOdometer()` to mint 4-char player IDs (`Aa`..`Zz`). Since `/p/` already tracks active players, this can stay as-is unless you want to move the odometer out of `W` registers entirely (e.g., to an `/a/` file or server-only counter).
* **`W5` (Boots Enabled), `W6` (Move Points Register), `W7` (PvP Tag Register):** Actively used for game rules.
* **`W8` & `W9`:** Completely unused and open.


