### 6. Quick Punch-Code Cleanup Checklist (From Reading `qandyland-univac.js`)
Before writing a lot of game scripts in the new map editor, there are a few small quirks in `qandyland-univac.js` worth ironing out so your punch code behaves consistently:

1. **Inconsistent `ifnot` (`Xn`) reset:** `Xi`, `Xl`, `Xe`, `Xm`, `Vc`, `Xt`, `Vx`, `Vy`, `Vz` all reset `ifnot = false;` after executing, whereas **`Vm`, `Vd`, and `Vt` do not**. That means `XnVdCa` or `XnVtA100` currently leaves `Xn` armed for the next command.
2. **Single-player (`gfxTickRate = 0`) vs Server `UNIVAC`:** Right now `cylon-gfx.js` doesn't run `UNIVAC` locally when offline/single-player—it runs `CylonScript`. Since `qandyland-univac.js` already has `window.UNIVAC` browser exports at the bottom, you have the option later to run the *exact same* punch-code engine client-side when `gfxTickRate === 0`!
3. **Small opcode rough edges:**
